## 2. Structural path (descriptors → candidate (n,m) sets)

Rule-based mapping, no image required. Each rule emits `(n, m, confidence, note)`.
Composition rules: conjunction of independent descriptors multiplies scores; conflicting
descriptors emit multiple candidates.

| # | Descriptor pattern | Rule | Output candidates |
|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | "k-fold symmetric" / "k arms" / "k-petal" | `n = k` (fundamental); aliases `n ∈ divisors(k)` at reduced score | `(k, ?, high for n)` |
| R2 | "q concentric rings of features" | `m = q` (rings are nodal-circle analogues) or `m = q+1` if rim counts as a node | `(0 or k, q∼q+1, medium)` |
| R3 | "mirror symmetric about d diameters" | `n = d` or `2d` (mirror symmetry implies standing wave `cos(nθ)`, any n̂ with that mirror count) | `(d, ?, medium)` |
| R4 | "k-arm spiral (logarithmic)" | `n = k`, chirality recorded; m from bead count per arm if given, else `m ∈ {1..3}` medium-low | `(k, ·, medium)` |
| R5 | "p × q grid/array" | square/rectangular plate `(p, q)`; if p = q: add swapped degenerate note; if p,q prime: flag "no subharmonic ambiguity" | `(p, q, high geometric / low physical)` |
| R6 | "s-segment ratchet / gear" | `n = s` + **chirality** (ratchet teeth are chiral): report as traveling-wave candidate `cos(sθ − ωt)` | `(s, 1..2, medium)` |
| R7 | "dumbbell / two lobes" | `n = 1` dipole (two opposite lobes, one nodal diameter) — equivalently `n = 2` if lobes are opposite quadrants; disambiguate by counting nodal lines between lobes: 1 line → n=1, 2 lines → n=2 | `{(1,1),(2,1)} medium` |
| R8 | "fractal (Koch snowflake, Julia set, Sierpinski)" | no single mode: angular spectrum is a **comb** at harmonics of the base order (Koch: base n=3 or 6; Julia `z²+c` spirals: n=2 arms typical) + continuum. Report `(n_base, ·, low)` and state "broadband, non-modal" | `(n_base, ?, low)` |
| R9 | "concentric ring + central disc" (figure+disc) | two-component glyph (§4.2): disc = `n=0` boundary anchor; interior figure decoded separately by R1–R8 | composite candidate |
| R10 | "tetrahedral / 3-fold 3-D pictogram" | projective symmetry of tetrahedron `T_d`: angular orders `{3}` in the view plane, but true object is 3-D → flag "2-D projection aliases multiple 3-D orientations"; candidates `(3, m∈{1,2})` | `(3, ·, low-medium)` |
| R11 | "N discrete dots/circles arranged on k arms or rings" | `n = k`; `m ≈ N/k` per arm (or per ring: `m = #rings`); divisors of N that factor as `n·m` give the alias set | factor-pair list |

