## 3. Ambiguity quantification and scoring

### 3.1 Match score
For each candidate mode `μ = (n, m, class)`:
```
S(μ) = w_ang · s_ang(n) + w_rad · s_rad(n,m) + w_node · (−ε_node(n,m)) + w_prior · log π(class)
```
- `s_ang(n) = A(n)² / Σ_{ℓ≥1} A(ℓ)²` — normalized angular power share.
- `s_rad(n,m) = max(0, corr(P̂_n, |J_n(α_{n,m}·r/R)|))` — Bessel template correlation.
- `ε_node` = RMS residual of measured nodal radii vs. `α_{n,j}/α_{n,m}` table (§1.3).
- `π(class)` = resonator-class prior (